  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676038",
      "title": "Getting Started with User Login",
      "lectureOrder": 94,
      "videoOrder": 87,
      "sourceHash": "e8600175c0e9d77066a235eb620082a8177232bc758bc1fcdc8caa1c3b41b2c5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "Now that we're able to create users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 6.33,
          "en": "we of course also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.33,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "that we add some login logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "and we can authenticate users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "and that's therefore what we'll do next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "For that, back in the auth.server.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "I'll add another new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 21.45,
          "en": "another async function called login, which is exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.45,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "And therefore again, we can use object destructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "And then here we wanna do what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "Well, we wanna check whether we find a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 34.26,
          "en": "for that email address, and if we find one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.26,
          "end": 37.893,
          "en": "whether the password of that user is equal to this password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 40.5,
          "en": "Now for finding a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 43.14,
          "en": "we can use the same logic as for signing up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.14,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "This line of code can be copied into this log in function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 50.733,
          "en": "This will find us a user in the database for that email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.05,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "Now, if we don't have an existing user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 56.22,
          "en": "then we have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.22,
          "end": 60.15,
          "en": "Before for signing up, we had a problem if we had a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.15,
          "end": 61.62,
          "en": "Now the opposite is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.62,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "If we don't have a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 67.713,
          "en": "well then signing up with that user is rather difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.76,
          "end": 71.91,
          "en": "So in that case I again wanna generate an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.91,
          "end": 73.71000000000001,
          "en": "and throw that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.71000000000001,
          "end": 78.15,
          "en": "and I'll give that error a status code of let's say 401.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.15,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "Because yeah, it is some invalid user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "but it's also an authentication problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "if you try to sign up with a non-existent email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "So I'll use this status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "Ultimately, it doesn't matter though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "because I'm not sending it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 94.263,
          "en": "as an HTTP error response anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "But then here I'll tweak the error message and say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 100.62,
          "en": "Could not log you in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.62,
          "end": 104.82300000000001,
          "en": "please check the provided credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.68,
          "end": 108.15,
          "en": "So that's the first check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.15,
          "end": 111.033,
          "en": "Do we have a user for that email?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.96000000000001,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "If we make it past this check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "then we know that we do have a user for that email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 121.56,
          "en": "So then we want to compare passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.56,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "Now since we retrieved a user here in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 126.52,
          "en": "we can of course add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.508,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "and check if existingUser.password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 132.633,
          "en": "is not equal to the password entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 135.663,
          "en": "But this would not work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.56,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "because keep in mind that in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 142.77,
          "en": "we store the password like this, it's hashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.77,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "It's not the password entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 146.22,
          "en": "It's not readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.22,
          "end": 149.043,
          "en": "So comparing it like this would always fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 153.27,
          "en": "Instead, this bcryptjs package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.27,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "which we used for hashing also gives us a compare function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 158.91,
          "en": "which is able to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 163.74,
          "en": "whether a plain text password could lead to a hash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.74,
          "end": 167.52,
          "en": "So it's able to compare a plain text password to a hash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.52,
          "end": 171.72,
          "en": "and therefore here I'll add a new constant, passwordCorrect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.72,
          "end": 174.87,
          "en": "where I await the result of calling compare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.87,
          "end": 176.95,
          "en": "from that bcryptjs package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 180.69,
          "en": "and where we then compare the raw password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 183.06,
          "en": "to the hash password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.06,
          "end": 185.583,
          "en": "so to the password on existingUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.67,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "And then we can check if the password is not correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "in which case we again have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.74,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "And in which case I'll throw the same error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "And again we could definitely write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "some separate function that allows us to reuse this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 204.963,
          "en": "Here, I'll just copy and paste it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.13,
          "end": 209.73,
          "en": "So we have these two error cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.73,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "that we don't find a user for the email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 214.53,
          "en": "or that the password is wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.53,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "But if we make it past these cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 219.15,
          "en": "we know that everything is correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.15,
          "end": 222.75,
          "en": "And then we do what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 225.84,
          "en": "Well, then we want to create such a session cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.84,
          "end": 227.19299999999998,
          "en": "which I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
